watch-pin-alive — the regression guard for #s36: a pinned server that ACCEPTS a
TCP connection while the tunnel probe fails is a wedged router, not a dead
server, and recovery runs as it always did.

Same world as watch-pin-dead, but the direct connect to 203.0.113.10:443 is
answered (no .rc, so the shim exits 0). The recovery stamp (watch.restart) sits
in 2100, so the cooldown holds the reload off and the tick stays quick and its
tree deterministic: what the case pins is that the pinned-dead arm did NOT
fire — no watch.hold and no watchdog-hold audit line (log/ is not compared,
so the cooldown line itself is not asserted).
